@@@ meta
id: ARR-M-09
topic: Arrays
difficulty: Medium
type: FIND_THE_BUG
title: In-Place Merge of Two ECU Event Logs Loses Entries
tags: embedded, merge-sorted-arrays, in-place, two-pointers, event-log
@@@ statement_md
A gateway ECU collects timestamped events from two sub-ECUs. Both logs are already sorted by timestamp. Log A sits in a buffer that has room for **both** logs, so the gateway merges log B into it **in place**, filling from the back so that no temporary buffer is needed. On equal timestamps the entry from log A must come first.

On most test drives the merged log looks right. But when the second ECU starts logging **earlier** than the first one (for example, it wakes up first after a CAN wake-up frame), the start of the merged log contains wrong entries and B's earliest events are missing. When log A is empty, the output is all zeros.

Find and fix the bug. Do not change the input or output format.

**Input**
- Line 1: `m n`, the sizes of log A and log B.
- Next `m` lines: log A entries `timestamp code` (code in hex).
- Next `n` lines: log B entries, same format.

**Output**
- The merged log, one entry per line: `timestamp CODE` (code as 4 hex digits).

**Example**
```
Input:
2 2
50 00A1
60 00A2
10 00B1
20 00B2

Output:
10 00B1
20 00B2
50 00A1
60 00A2
```
@@@ constraints_md
- `0 <= m, n <= 1000`
- `0 <= timestamp <= 4294967295`, `0 <= code <= 0xFFFF`
- Both logs are sorted by timestamp (non-decreasing).
@@@ starter_code
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdint.h>

#define MAX_A 1000
#define MAX_B 1000

typedef struct {
    uint32_t ts;     /* timestamp in ms */
    uint16_t code;   /* event code      */
} event_t;

static event_t log_a[MAX_A + MAX_B];   /* has room for both logs */
static event_t log_b[MAX_B];

/* Merge sorted b[0..n-1] into sorted a[0..m-1] (capacity m + n), in place.
 * On equal timestamps the entry from a comes first. */
static void merge_logs(event_t *a, int m, const event_t *b, int n)
{
    int i = m - 1;          /* last entry of a       */
    int j = n - 1;          /* last entry of b       */
    int k = m + n - 1;      /* last free slot of a   */

    while (i >= 0 && j >= 0) {
        if (a[i].ts > b[j].ts)
            a[k--] = a[i--];
        else
            a[k--] = b[j--];
    }
    while (i >= 0)
        a[k--] = a[i--];
}

static int read_events(event_t *dst, int count)
{
    for (int i = 0; i < count; i++) {
        unsigned ts, code;
        if (scanf("%u %x", &ts, &code) != 2) return 0;
        dst[i].ts = (uint32_t)ts;
        dst[i].code = (uint16_t)code;
    }
    return 1;
}

int main(void)
{
    int m, n;
    if (scanf("%d %d", &m, &n) != 2) return 0;
    if (m < 0 || m > MAX_A || n < 0 || n > MAX_B) return 0;
    if (!read_events(log_a, m) || !read_events(log_b, n)) return 0;

    merge_logs(log_a, m, log_b, n);

    for (int i = 0; i < m + n; i++)
        printf("%u %04X\n", (unsigned)log_a[i].ts, (unsigned)log_a[i].code);
    return 0;
}
